== PREPARATION
> Take the salvage office door to the salvage office   [success, watch 1]
  | A ledger lies open on a trestle beside a sketch of foundry machinery. A licence is pinned above it, its seal still bright.
  | A chalked note says Edda is out at Foundry yard under the salvage company's permit, which runs until watch 41.
> Take the salvage office door to Reedwake quay   [success, watch 2]
  * Wren hurries over to you. 'Are you going up to Censer Hill foundry? Have you seen Pell?'
== OUT BY THE RIDGE
> Take the causeway path to Willow causeway   [success, watch 8]
> Take the ridge track to Chalk ridge   [success, watch 11]
> Take the track up to the yard to Foundry yard   [success, watch 14]
  | Rusting tram rails cross an ash-grown yard. A roofless arch opens into the upper works. A surveyor's scratches mark a climb up the hoist side; without a proper harness it is too exposed.
> Ask Edda what they are salvaging   [success, watch 15]
  "'The bronze tram bearing, not someone's grandmother,' says Edda. 'It's in Hoist room. Bring me the actual thing and I'll pay six coin from my own purse. The salvage company's permit runs out at watch 41; after that I go home, and I am not taking my crew down there to chase it. If anything else finds its way out with you, I don't ask questions.'"
> Examine a copy of the permit, nailed to a post   [success, watch 16]
  * The salvage company's permit covers the bronze tram bearing and the old machinery. It does not cover the dead, or anything buried with them.
> Take the roofless arch to Surveyor's vestibule   [success, watch 17]
> Take the workshop doorway to Bell workshop   [success, watch 18]
> Pick the stores padlock   [success, watch 19]
> Take the stores door to Dry stores   [success, watch 20]
